  "g": 2.2,
  "src": "No published Secchi depth for Lake Tekapo was found (searched 2026-11-05), so Kd is Lake Pukaki's, from that glacial-flour lake's Secchi depth (cities/lake-pukaki/city.json). Rinf keeps Pukaki's brightness with Tekapo's own hue: in the LINZ 10 m mosaic (median of 400 m windows at four mid-lake points, linearised) Tekapo is 0.0072, 0.206, 0.405 (green over blue 0.51) against Pukaki's 0.0037, 0.120, 0.250 (0.48) measured the same way; the mosaic is colour-balanced sheet by sheet, so only the hue is carried over."
